(Conditional evidence) Tj T*
(Definition: P\(A | B\) = P\(A and B\) / P\(B\), provided P\(B\) > 0.) Tj T*
(The denominator restricts the sample space to the observed event B.) Tj T*
(For disjoint causes A and not A, P\(B\) = P\(B | A\)P\(A\) + P\(B | not A\)P\(not A\).) Tj T*
(This partition assumption is needed to normalize both possible causes.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
