(A diagnostic example) Tj T*
(A condition affects 1 percent of a population.) Tj T*
(A test has sensitivity 90 percent and specificity 95 percent.) Tj T*
(True positive mass is 0.01 * 0.90 = 0.009.) Tj T*
(False positive mass is 0.99 * 0.05 = 0.0495.) Tj T*
(Thus P\(condition | positive\) = 0.009 / 0.0585 = 2 / 13.) Tj T*
(The small base rate matters even though the test is usually correct.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
