BT /F1 12 Tf 54 730 Td 19 TL
(Sequential evidence and its limit) Tj T*
(For two conditionally independent observations, multiply their likelihood ratios.) Tj T*
(Independence must hold conditional on A and separately conditional on not A.) Tj T*
(Duplicating the same positive test result does not provide independent evidence.) Tj T*
(Exercise: with prior odds 1:9 and independent likelihood ratios 3 and 2, find posterior odds.) Tj T*
(Solution: posterior odds are 6:9 = 2:3, so posterior probability is 2 / 5.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
